# WLISTTU.KEY - gestures while a move is busy, keys taken while the
# list window holds the capture, the pieces of a row and of the header,
# and the empty text's, over the seed's three items;
# TEST/GOLDEN/WIN/WLISTTU.SNP.
S START
# SHIFT-G: the line down comes during the End move, its SB_ENDSCROLL
# after it: nothing recorded, no move.
K SHIFT-G
S SBUSYG
K T
# CTRL-G: the gesture's move, posted before the End move, is taken
# while the End move is busy and dropped; a gesture after it moves.
K CTRL-G
S CBUSYG
K P
S CBUSYP
# H: a Down key taken while the list window holds the capture is
# dropped; once the capture is released, Down moves.
K DOWN
K H
S CAPTURE
K DOWN
S FREED
# The pieces of the first row, ID order: the ID, the maker, the
# right-aligned quantity and the status; no column 8.
K T
K SHIFT-0
S PIECE0
K SHIFT-2
S PIECE2
K SHIFT-5
S PIECE5
K SHIFT-7
S PIECE7
K SHIFT-8
S PIECE8
# The header's: its right-aligned "ID" in a left column, trimmed.
K CTRL-0
S HEAD0
K CTRL-5
S HEAD5
# A marked row's item data.
K DOWN
K SHIFT-1
S MARKED
# The empty text: item data WL_WHOLE, cut with the NULL table, one
# column.
K F6
S EMPTY
K SHIFT-0
S EPIECE0
K SHIFT-1
S EPIECE1
K F6
S FULL
